      "body": "This behavior is expected and was intentionally maintained during the recent routing layer rewrite in #2096. Queryable information is only reduced in gateways that need to represent multiple south-bound notes. The protocol treats each queryable (re-)declaration on the same keyexpr as an info\u2014i.e. completeness, distance\u2014update. This behavior is the same for session-to-runtime and on-the-wire queryable declarations.\n\n@leon-somana: does this behavior break a specific use case for you?",
