      "updated_at": "2026-06-12T22:18:39Z",
      "body": "Sorry, my terminology was wrong when I said \"two storage plugins\". I meant two storages set-up against the standard storage manager plugin instantiation.\n\nPlugins don't share the same session, but multiple storages _do_ share the same session within the storage plugin.\n\n```\n- plugins/zenoh-plugin-storage-manager/src/lib.rs:132 \u2014 one session per plugin: let session = Arc::new(zenoh::session::init(runtime.clone()).wait()?);\n- spawn_storage (lib.rs:289) passes self.session.clone() into create_and_start_storage for every storage.\n- Each storage then declares its queryable on that shared session with its own flag: src/storages_mgt/service.rs:153-154 \u2192 self.session.declare_queryable(...).complete(self.configuration.complete).\n```\n\nSo this is specifically replicable with zenohd + 2 storages.\n\n\n```\n  {\n    plugins: {\n      storage_manager: {\n        volumes: {\n          rocksdb: { /* ... */ },\n          s3:      { backend: \"s3\", /* ... */ },\n        },\n        storages: {\n          primary: {\n            key_expr: \"state/**\",\n            volume:   \"rocksdb\",\n            complete: true,        // authoritative \u2014 answers AllComplete\n          },\n          fallback: {\n            key_expr: \"state/**\",   // identical key_expr\n            volume:   \"s3\",\n            complete: false,       // best-effort \u2014 should NOT answer AllComplete\n          },\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  }",
      "author_association": "NONE",
